zsh in the 5BSD base system
==========================

contrib/zsh is imported from the zsh 5.9.2 source release from
https://www.zsh.org/pub/zsh-5.9.2.tar.xz.
SHA256: 36fa734374b44783582cec09bcd67822e2f992c779ec1624ab5596df078d2f81
This matches shells/zsh/distinfo in the 5BSD ports checkout.
Local source changes adapt the maintained ports fixes for RLIMIT_VMM,
terminal restoration on timeout, and diff -u completion. Character conversion
also treats a positive iconv result (non-reversible conversion) as out of
range, preserving strict errors and byte fallback in parameter expansion with
BSD iconv. The resource-limit manual is updated, and .gitignore retains
release-generated build inputs.
The _mdo completion is taken from the same ports checkout. The W02/W03
job-control test harnesses acknowledge an end marker before their zpty session
leader exits, preventing BSD tty revocation from discarding unread output.

The native bsd.prog.mk build installs /bin/zsh, its functions and license
in the runtime package, so minimal installations and installation media
have the default login shell. Manuals follow the standard base MAN option.
No ports libraries, configure step, Python, GNU make, target executables,
or network access are required during buildworld. Normal compilation uses
make's parallel job count. Modules are linked into zsh; shared base libraries
are still used unless WITHOUT_DYNAMICROOT is selected.

The upstream license is MIT-style, with file-specific exceptions. The optional
GPL-licensed completions _darcs, _osc, _qdbus, and _zypper are retained in
the vendor source but excluded from installed functions. GDBM and PCRE are
not built; their test groups are removed from the vendor import by
import-build.py. The privileged-mode tests remain because they cover built-in
shell behavior. The upstream license is installed in /usr/share/doc/zsh/LICENCE.

/bin/sh remains the system script interpreter and /rescue/sh remains available
for recovery. Service accounts keep their existing restricted shells. Account
creation defaults to /bin/zsh unless the administrator explicitly selects a
shell or has configured an override. The installer Shell action and final
configuration shell also use zsh. Existing password databases are not rewritten
by building or installing these source templates; migrating an existing account
requires an explicit chsh/pw change after /bin/zsh has been installed.

/etc/zshrc initializes interactive completion and key bindings. Root and new
users receive .zprofile and .zshrc. zsh does not read .profile or .shrc; users
migrating existing accounts should move applicable personal settings into zsh's
startup files rather than blindly sourcing a file written for another shell.

Refreshing generated files
--------------------------
The checked-in headers are generated using upstream's own scripts. They keep
normal and cross builds independent of autoconf and the build host's ability to
execute target programs. Integer types use the target ABI, MACHTYPE comes from
MACHINE_ARCH, and signal/errno tables are regenerated from target headers.

For an upstream refresh on 5BSD, create a fresh object directory under /usr/obj
and run the vendor configure script there with:

  --prefix=/usr --bindir=/bin --sysconfdir=/etc
  --enable-zshenv=/etc/zshenv --enable-zprofile=/etc/zprofile
  --enable-zshrc=/etc/zshrc --enable-zlogin=/etc/zlogin
  --enable-zlogout=/etc/zlogout --disable-dynamic --disable-gdbm
  --disable-pcre --enable-multibyte
  --enable-fndir=/usr/share/zsh/functions --disable-site-fndir
  --enable-additional-fpath=/usr/local/share/zsh/site-functions
  --with-term-lib=ncursesw

Copy this directory's modules.conf to that object directory as config.modules.
Review available features and module choices when updating versions, then run:

  make prep
  make -C Src headers
  make -C Src -f Makemod zshpaths.h zshxmods.h bltinmods.list version.h \
      patchlevel.h main.epro
  make -C Src/Zle zle_widget.h widgets.list thingies.list
  make -C Src/Modules curses_keys.h
  python3.12 /usr/src/bin/zsh/import-build.py /usr/src/contrib/zsh \
      /usr/obj/PATH-TO-CONFIGURED-BUILD /usr/src/bin/zsh

Review config.h for newly introduced host-dependent feature checks, and audit
new function licenses before accepting the update. Test the native binary with
contrib/zsh/Test/runtests.zsh, including completion and ZLE tests. Upstream's
header-generation makefiles serialize work; the native compilation does not.

Validation notes
----------------
Native amd64 compilation, a NO_ROOT staged install, isolated pw account
creation, startup/completion checks, and the upstream test groups were checked.
The retained suite has 63 groups: 62 passed and privileged execution was
skipped because root access was unavailable. The PCRE and GDBM groups were
removed because those modules are not included in the base shell. The W02/W03 harness fix passed ten consecutive runs of each
complete group and a final run of each checked-in version. A system-call trace
and a shell-independent pty reproducer confirmed output loss on terminal
revocation; job-control commands and expected output were not changed.
The privileged group still requires execution from a root shell. Cross builds
and a complete world/image build have not been validated by this component check.
